{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "32c81d6c-b685-4c77-bfce-3f14c30114cc",
    "name": "Quipu Nexus",
    "description": "Complete REST API collection for Quipu Nexus (port 3040) — natural-language knowledge-graph search. Blends structured search (entity anchoring + intent classification + path planning -> Cypher via Synapse) and unstructured search (vector similarity over Milvus doc embeddings), returning ranked subgraphs.\n\nCollection variables:\n- {{baseUrl}}  — default http://localhost:3040\n- {{token}}    — bearer JWT sent as Authorization header\n- {{tenantId}} — tenant identifier (X-Tenant-ID header; fallback when not derivable from the JWT)\n\nNotes:\n- All /nexus endpoints share the same SearchRequest body (fabricId, query, topK, skipUnstructured) and produce application/vnd.quipu.nexus-search+json;version=1.0.0.\n- /nexus/schema/traversable/** endpoints produce application/vnd.quipu.nexus-traversable+json;version=1.0.0.\n- /schema/** (vectorization) endpoints produce application/vnd.quipu.nexus-vectorization+json;version=1.0.0. POST /schema/vectorize/{fabricId} returns 202 Accepted (or 409 Conflict if a job is already running) and takes no body. DELETE /schema/{fabricId} returns 204 No Content.\n- /schema-family responses return the raw MinIO path-graph object; an absent object means an empty graph by design (no KGS fallback).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "56383100",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/56383100-32c81d6c-b685-4c77-bfce-3f14c30114cc?source=collection_link"
  },
